//BUG="a return inside a for is treated as enough, though the range may be empty"
//ERR any

// The `for` counterpart of 27_the_only_return_is_inside_a_while.cpl. `0..0` is
// an empty range — see 04_control_flow/11_for_over_an_empty_range.cpl — so the
// body never runs. No `for` should count as returning, whatever its bounds look
// like; the check stays structural rather than reasoning about the range.

fn f n
    for i 0..n
        ret i

fn main
    out "{f(0)}"
